    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d769">

                <pb facs="0845" n="835" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg835"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">093.112/659a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the
                        Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-06T14:00:00-04:00">March 6, 1944—2
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>491. Personal for the Ambassador. We do not yet have a definite and final
                    solution of the decorations problem insofar as the military is concerned,
                    although, as it now stands, battlefield decorations may be permitted but
                    officers engaged in supply operations, such as lend lease, <pb facs="0846"
                        n="836" xml:id="pg836"/> would not be permitted to accept. Additional
                    information will follow as soon as possible on that aspect of the problem.</p>
                <p>As to civilian officials of the Government, there is a statute<anchor n="84"
                        xml:id="d769-f1"/> Which definitely precludes acceptance unless authorized
                    by Act of Congress.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d769-f1" n="84" xml:id="d769-f1-content">
                <p>Approved January 31, 1881; 21 Stat. 604.</p>
            </note>
